Changelog: 17-10-2026 09:27:13

Fixed. The app's folder in the suite is apps/check (was apps/bazzite-test) and its package is bazzite_check (was
bc250_gui): the suite's naming convention (owner, 17-10-2026), a short folder name and the package named after
the app without the BC-250 prefix; the short name is check rather than test, so that no folder is called test.
With the folder go its key in the portal, its chapter of the wiki (apps/check/), its installer test and its
release tags: check-v<x.y.z> from the next release on, which is also what the app's update check looks for. The
installed app keeps its name, its launcher bc250-bazzite-test, its folder under /opt, its settings, its results
and its logs; the portal moves its record of the installed copy to the new key. The launch option the In-Game page
hands out for Steam names the new package (-m bazzite_check.gamemon); one copied before this names the old one and
is to be copied again (nobody runs one yet, owner, 17-10-2026).

Changelog: 17-10-2026 05:35:55

Release 0.3.0.

Changelog: 17-10-2026 00:48:59

Added. Test 52, HDMI-CEC Services (GPU and graphics): whether the services behind the TV control run. Valve's CEC
daemon (cecd, a user service) when enabled; HDMI CEC Manager's background service (bc250-hdmi-cec-watch) and boot
service (bc250-hdmi-cec-boot, with its udev rule) when installed; Bazzite's dGPU CEC services when enabled. A service
that is installed or enabled but not running, or failed, is a warning with the journalctl command to read why; one
that is not installed is only reported, and so is a stopped cecd or boot service without a CEC adapter. Without a
desktop session the user services' state is reported as unknown. In the catalog and both chapters of the manual.

