Changelog: 11-10-2026 07:28:24

Release 0.1.1. More hints and tips when warnings or failures are found in the logs

Changelog: 11-10-2026 01:18:47

Tests 15, 16 and 17 now explain the journal lines they show instead of only listing them. After the lines comes a
hint per kind of line, with the number of lines it covers: what it means and what to do about it. Real faults come
first (GPU hangs and page faults, display timeouts, missing firmware, NVMe timeouts, disk errors, MCEs, out of
memory, crashes, services that cannot run from a home folder, USB failures), then known harmless messages
(shutdown transactions, KDE Wallet, Bluetooth, D-Bus activation, passwords, Plasma, PipeWire, KWin, printer status,
desktop portal). A failed unit gets the journalctl and systemctl disable commands for that unit, and the remaining
lines are grouped per program with the command to read them. The table is LOG_ADVICE in test-bazzite.sh, and
tests/test_log_advice.py runs it. The raw lines, the exclusions and the test results are unchanged.

Changelog: 10-10-2026 20:56:48

Release 0.1.0. Initial release

Changelog: 10-10-2026 19:25:36

TTM hints follow the kernel: amdgpu sizes GTT from ttm.pages_limit and caps it at the system RAM on this APU.
Test 37 now reports the real dynamic ceiling (the GTT total) instead of the parameter, says when ttm.pages_limit is
above the RAM and therefore has no effect, and gives the small-split ceiling from the live split and GTT instead of
the fixed 8.25 GiB. The stress test no longer always suggests ttm.pages_limit=2621440 when GTT runs full: that could
lower a higher limit, and --append-if-missing may add a second ttm.pages_limit instead of changing it. When GTT is already as
large as the RAM, or the limit is already 3014656, it points at the memory use and the swap layout instead;
otherwise it suggests 3014656 (the value of test 37) with --replace or --append. The saturated-VRAM hint names
bc250_memcfg instead of a BIOS setting the board does not expose.

Changelog history: entries no longer name the third-party CU manager the early versions read.

Changelog: 10-10-2026 13:33:27

Print results now opens the saved PNG in the system image viewer and keeps a clickable thumbnail with its folder
in the app header.

