Changelog: 09-10-2026 17:30:50

A benchmark-only run (test 42 without test 21) no longer scores a runtime CU unlock as stock. Test 42 took its CU
count from test 21 and otherwise from the kernel's probe-time active_cu_number, which stays 24 after a runtime
unlock, so the Configuration line, the history and the CU factor of the Extended score fell back to 24. Test 21's
live WGP-mask read (umr, read-only, as root) is now the function read_live_cus, and test 42 calls it when test 21
did not run; the probe value remains the last resort. Test 21's checks and output are unchanged: the register
reads moved into the function as they were.

