Minor improvement in the readme.

Changelog: 06-10-2026 08:54:06

Packaging (roadmap item 2, first release): added .github/workflows/release.yml. Every push to main
builds a release tarball and publishes it as a GitHub Release with a sha256 file and generated
release notes. The patch version is auto-bumped from bc250_gui/__init__.py's __version__ or the
latest v* tag, whichever is higher, so routine releases need no source edit - bump __version__ only
for a deliberate major/minor jump, and add "[skip-version]" to a commit message to skip releasing
it. The workflow runs sanity checks (bash -n on the engine, compileall on the Python) and packages
a staged copy of the tracked tree in which __init__.py carries the released version (so About shows
what was downloaded) and development/tools/build_info.py has been run: the generated
bc250_gui/_build_info.py (build date + SHA-256 of test-bazzite.sh) makes the download run as a
release build with the engine integrity check active. The staged tree gets normalized permissions
(755 directories, go-w files - git archive can emit group-writable modes, which that check refuses)
and the tarball stores root:root ownership, so "sudo tar -xzf ... -C /opt" yields exactly the
root-owned tree the check requires; verified in an Ubuntu container. Also fixed build_info.py,
which resolved the repository root one directory short (development/ instead of the root) since it
moved to development/tools, and removed the version-tag.yml stub.

README: the "no release yet" placeholder under "Download and install" is replaced by the real
Bazzite instructions (the GUI is the product; the command line is development-only): download and
verify with sha256sum -c, extract to /opt with sudo plus a stable /opt/bc250-bazzite-test symlink,
one-time venv in ~/.local/share/bc250-bazzite-test/venv with pip install --upgrade -r requirements.txt, run
with python -m bc250_gui, optional test tools via development/tools/install-requirements.sh, and
update and uninstall steps. A note explains why /opt: a release build refuses to run
test-bazzite.sh unless the file and every folder above it are owned by root and writable by root
only, so a copy in the home directory fails that check on purpose. The venv, settings and history
live in the home directory and survive updates.

Changelog: 06-10-2026 03:00:00

MangoHud style: the FPS row label and the logging indicator dot are white instead of black (the
previous trick of matching them to the background failed because MangoHud draws its colors fully
opaque over the translucent box). The dot cannot be hidden or made transparent at all: MangoHud
forces every configured color opaque and has no setting for the indicator, which appears whenever
logging runs — and logging stays on so FPS reaches the graphs.

