Changelog: 06-10-2026 02:20:00

MangoHud styling, take three (previous attempts kept being polluted by Bazzite's shipped MangoHud
defaults and presets merging back in). "Style MangoHud like the overlay" now writes a complete
config file owned by the app (~/.config/bc250-bazzite-test/MangoHud.conf) and the game wrapper
passes it to MangoHud directly (MANGOHUD_CONFIGFILE), so nothing else can mix into the look and the
user's own MangoHud.conf is left alone (an older appended block is cleaned up). The layout is a
narrow two-column box: FPS (labeled "FPS" instead of the engine name), GPU, clock, temperature,
power, CPU, VRAM — as close to one metric per line as MangoHud allows. Background lightened to 0.5
so it is translucent instead of near-black. FPS logging for the graphs is always on in this file.

Changelog: 06-10-2026 02:10:00

MangoHud style, second round (the first looked nothing like the overlay): the managed block now uses
MangoHud's modern layout (legacy_layout=0) so the rows appear exactly in the overlay's order — FPS,
GPU, CPU, clock, temperature, power, VRAM — and explicitly turns off everything MangoHud shows by
default that the overlay does not have: the frametime value and graph, the throttling block
(Power/Current/Temp/Other), the DXVK/engine row and the text outline. Background made slightly more
opaque (0.85) for readability.

Changelog: 06-10-2026 02:00:00

Game details page: "Style MangoHud like the overlay" button. It rewrites the style keys in
