Changelog: 06-10-2026 01:10:00

Fix: the overlay could stay invisible. On Wayland (Bazzite's KDE desktop) a normal window cannot be
positioned or kept on top, so the overlay now runs on XWayland (xcb, with wayland as fallback) where
KWin honors both. It also places itself on the game's screen, re-raises itself every few seconds (a
game that goes fullscreen later would otherwise cover it) and its errors now reach Steam's game log
("gamemon: overlay started (pid …)" confirms it launched). Game mode (gamescope) still cannot show
external windows — use the desktop session to see the overlay.

Changelog: 06-10-2026 00:55:00

On-screen overlay: a new per-game "Show overlay" toggle on the Game details page. While the game runs,
the wrapper shows the live FPS, CPU/GPU load, clock, temperature, power and VRAM in a small translucent
box top-left of the screen — like MangoHud's HUD but in the app's style: rounded corners, a thin purple
border and a purple FPS accent. The overlay never takes focus and lets all mouse input through, runs as
its own process (an overlay problem can never touch the game) and closes itself with the game. Being a
normal window it shows over windowed and borderless-fullscreen games on the desktop; gamescope's game
mode and exclusive fullscreen can cover it. Off by default; saved per game in games.ini.

