Changelog: 05-10-2026 22:15:00

GUI v0.12.0 — iteration 12, in-game monitoring:
- New gamemon wrapper for the Steam launch options, used like MangoHud: put
  "<python> -m bc250_gui.gamemon %command%" in the game's Properties > Launch options. It starts the
  game unchanged and records FPS (from MangoHud's log), the game's CPU and GPU share, total CPU/GPU
  load and the GPU clock, temperature, power and VRAM into one CSV per session in
  ~/.local/share/bc250-bazzite-test/game-logs/. Pure /proc and sysfs reads as the normal user: no
  root, no helpers, and a sampling problem can never kill the game. Steam's SIGTERM is forwarded so
  the game closes cleanly.
- Per-game settings (recording on/off, sample interval 1-60 s) in
  ~/.config/bc250-bazzite-test/games.ini, shared between the wrapper and the GUI (gamecfg.py, plain
  configparser so the wrapper runs without Qt).
- New In-game page: the launch line with a Copy button, the games seen so far with their settings,
  and every session as a graph (FPS, game/total load, GPU clock, temperature, power, VRAM — new game
  panels in the graph dialog, with a session summary). Help and README describe it.

