Changelog: 03-10-2026 15:00:00

GUI v0.9.7 (integrity of the test engine and the history):
- Before every run the app checks the test engine: the file and every folder above it must be owned by
  root and not writable by others, and in a release build its SHA-256 must equal the one recorded at build
  time (new tools/build_info.py writes bc250_gui/_build_info.py, git-ignored). A release build refuses to
  run a changed or unprotected engine (red bar plus message); the git checkout runs in development mode with
  an orange banner listing the problems. The runner executes the resolved path that was checked.
- History database: mode 0600, folder 0700 (logs folder and log files too, log files opened without
  following symlinks); symlinked database refused; trusted_schema off; quick_check on start and no
  triggers/views allowed. A damaged or tampered database is kept as history.db.damaged-<date> and a new
  one is started, with a message.
- Message boxes with paths or file contents always show plain text; the build date comes from the build
  info when present.
- Help: new "Integrity of the tests" section and a note on the history check. DEVELOPMENT.md: security section.

