Changelog: 03-10-2026 09:15:00

Script + GUI v0.9.2:
- Benchmark baseline: one fixed location, /var/log/bc250-bazzite-test/bench-baseline.json, for every
  copy of the script and for the GUI. Before, it was saved next to the script, so a run from another
  copy (e.g. ~/test-bazzite.sh) found no baseline and the GUI showed no CPU/GPU score. A baseline saved
  next to the script by an older version is moved there on the next --bench run: it is read as the
  desktop user (a symlink to a root-only file is not copied) and only a JSON object with numeric
  results is accepted. Saving a baseline no longer writes or chowns anything in the user's folders as
  root. The GUI also still reads the old location until the move has happened.
- Settings: new section "Logs & history" with Clean up logs… (moved from the Overview); disabled
  while tests are running.
- Settings close button: small round ✕ like the window's title bar button (red on hover).
- Hints panel: more space and a divider between hints.
- Stats toolbar: "Ran" is now "Finished". Navigation: "Logs" is now "System logs".
- About: the description and "Report problems…" are on separate lines.

Changelog: 03-10-2026 08:30:00

Script + GUI v0.9.1 — security hardening:
- Script: the report copy to ~/Desktop/bc250-bazzite-test is now made entirely as the desktop user
  (folder and files); root no longer creates, copies into or chowns anything in the user's home, so a
  planted symlink there cannot make root overwrite or chown system files.
- Script: root's PATH is no longer extended with ~/.local/bin or Homebrew. Optional tools are found
  with find_tool: a tool that is user-writable (in ~/.local/bin, Homebrew, or anywhere not owned by
  root) is only ever run as the desktop user, never as root (stress-ng, vkpeak, memtest_vulkan, vkmark,
  glmark2, speedtest). fio reads the raw partition and needs root, so a user-installed fio is not used:
  the random 4K test is skipped with a hint to install fio system-wide (rpm-ostree install fio).
- GUI: text from outside the app (game window titles, log file references, CSV names and columns,
  speed test server/ISP, benchmark details) is HTML-escaped in labels, tooltips and chart titles.
- requirements.txt: PyQt6 and PyQt6-Charts >= 6.11 (current releases; no known CVEs for Python 3.13,
  PyQt6 6.11 / Qt 6.11 or sip 13.12 at the time of writing).

