  transparent background, in bold, instead of a filled light-blue bar.

Changelog: 30-09-2026 12:00:00

TEST 10 — NVMe Devices (extended):
- PCIe link: current speed/width vs. the drive's and the slot's maximum; warns when the link trained
  below what both support (bad contact), notes when the slot is the limit, shows the bandwidth ceiling.
- DRAM cache: DRAM-less drives are recognized by their Host Memory Buffer request (nvme id-ctrl HMPRE)
  and the kernel's "allocated N MiB host memory buffer"; warns when HMB is requested but not given.
- SMART health (nvme-cli JSON, else smartctl JSON, else hwmon temperature): critical warning bits,
  media errors, spare vs threshold, wear %, TB written, temperature vs the drive's own threshold,
  minutes spent above warning/critical temperature, unsafe shutdowns, error log entries.

TEST 43 — Disk Speed Test (new, opt-in with --disk-bench / --disk-write=GiB):
- Sequential read of 4 GiB from the system partition (dd, direct I/O, read-only), compared with the
  PCIe link ceiling. Random 4K read QD1/QD32 with fio --readonly when installed.
- Optional write test: GiB written to a No_COW temp file in /var/tmp (so btrfs compression cannot fake
  it) in 256 MiB chunks; per-chunk speed and drive temperature to bc250-disk-<ts>.csv. Reports start
  and end speed and the SLC cache size, or thermal throttling when the drop happens at the warning
  temperature. Stops at the critical temperature, checks free space first, removes the file on exit
  or Ctrl-C. The CSV is copied to the Desktop folder.

GUI v0.6.0:
- Storage page: test 43 button, "also test writes" + write size, Show graph for the disk CSV
  (write speed and temperature against GiB written). Confirmation before it runs; never part of
  Run all.

