Changelog: 28-09-2026 22:35:00

New tool — bc250-cu-bisect.sh:
- Per-Shader-Array CU bisect helper: tests one extra WGP (+2 CUs) per array while
  the other three stay at the known-good baseline (read from
  the CU manager's config, prompted otherwise).
- Per step: user applies the printed masks with an external CU manager, script
  verifies the routed count via its dashboard cache, runs a stress load
  (memtest_vulkan/vkpeak/vkmark/glmark2), scans the kernel log for GPU faults
  and asks about artifacts.
- Verdicts persisted to ~/.local/share/bc250-cu-bisect/results.tsv: crash-safe,
  resumes after the hard hang a bad WGP causes. Final summary suggests a
  combined mask from the passing arrays. A readable report is also copied to
  the Desktop (xdg-user-dir aware), like test-bazzite.sh does.

TESTs 15/16 — journal noise filters:
- input-remapper-control autoload probes (exit 1 = no preset for the device).
- kwin_wayland "Failed to find a working output layer configuration" and
  "Atomic modeset commit failed" (hotplug/DPMS retries).

README:
- New section: "Optional: finding your die's CU ceiling (bc250-cu-bisect.sh)".

Changelog: 28-09-2026 20:21:00

TEST 00 — BIOS identification (new):
- Reports BIOS vendor, version, date and release from /sys/class/dmi/id.
- Classifies the version string: stock ASRock (1.00-5.00, optional L/P
  prefix), modded (MeiMei/mod/unlock in the string, with a hint not to
  combine a modded BIOS with the initrd ACPI override), missing, or
  unrecognized.
- Notes that menu-unlock mods (e.g. the P3.00 "Chipset Menu" BIOS) keep
  the stock version string, so DMI cannot distinguish them from a
  factory BIOS — verified on a real board running that mod.

TEST 26 — ACPI table origin (new):
- Reports whether the ACPI tables were loaded from an initrd override
  (bc250-acpi-fix) or come from the BIOS, distinguishing "fix not
  applied" from "fix applied but failed to load".

TEST 36 — two more false ERRORs fixed, found via the new context blocks:
- The amdgpu HPD-init WARN at driver probe (amdgpu_dm_hpd_init): its
  register dump pushed the WARNING header outside the context window,
  so the benign filter missed it. The trace frames themselves are now
  matched.
- Userspace crashes logged by the kernel as "traps: <proc> general
  protection fault" (e.g. a KDE thumbnailer) are no longer treated as
  kernel faults; they belong to coredumpctl, which TEST 36 already
  reports separately.

Journal noise filters (TESTs 15/16), one-off session logout/login churn:
- PipeWire remote error reconnect spam.
- CUPS IPP_INTERNAL_ERROR reconnect loop and kded6 "Failed to
  reconnect Invalid argument".
- PreviewJob errors on since-deleted files.
- systemd-logind destructive-transaction races and the Varlink
  CreateSession failure during session teardown.

README:
- TEST 00 description now mentions BIOS reporting (stock vs modded).
- New optional section: ACPI fix without the P3.00 MeiMeiDXE v3 BIOS
  (e-tho/bc250-acpi-fix initrd override, Bazzite install steps,
  runtime 8-core unlock via rw-r-r-0644/bc250-core-unlock with
  caveats, duplicate-tables warning).
- VRAM advice notes that fanoush/bc250_memcfg makes the "Chipset Menu"
  modded BIOS obsolete for setting the UMA split.

